108 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (The year was 1945, the second world war was almost on its end. And the world sees for the first time, the most powerful weapon of mankind, a weapon so destructive that it can erase a city in a matter of seconds. Families, animals, histories, all that once was full of life has been ceased by the power of technology. Nagasaki and Hiroshima were two important cities at the time, and as said by the us government, this cities has the perfect conditions for the test of this weapons, and in order to show their power, the us state promote such a terrorist act against citizens, no soldiers killed in this cities, just people living their ordinary lives. And since then, Japanese society has changed, this collective trauma influenced a lot, and still has its influence nowadays.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
109 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (Art does not exist in void, it exists in a context, and in this context of trauma, these fears found their way to express themselves by the means of art. We could look at a lot of examples, but the most important for us to understand Serial Experiments Lain is the Japanese horror cinema in the late 90s to early 2000s.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
