113 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 58 0 R
/E (Because of the trauma, the way that Japanese artists viewed technology was a terrifying one. Lots of movies made after the two bombs showed distorted bodies, bodies that were violated by the high technology, ghosts that spawned in computers and televisions, and people losing their life perspective. Another important event that impacted the cinema was the lost decades. It was a period of economic stagnation and a moment where many young adults didn't have any perspective of finding a job, and this context created many individuals without any kind of hope for the future, and only saw darkness waiting around the corner. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
